20
00:03:41,852 --> 00:03:45,331
[Host] It means official recognition or certification.

21
00:03:45,931 --> 00:03:59,324
[Slow] 農林水産省が21日に発表したもので、かんがいとは、川や池から田んぼや畑に水を引くことです。

22
00:04:00,123 --> 00:04:09,195
[Host] The agriculture ministry announced it on the twenty-first — irrigation means drawing water from rivers or ponds into rice paddies and fields.

23
00:04:09,795 --> 00:04:11,883
[Vocab] 田んぼ

24
00:04:12,283 --> 00:04:16,411
[Host] It means a rice paddy — a flooded field where rice grows.

25
00:04:17,012 --> 00:04:28,411
[Slow] 葛西用水は、江戸時代の17世紀に作られた長い水路で、利根川から水を引いています。

26
00:04:29,211 --> 00:04:37,108
[Host] The Saitama canal was built in the seventeenth century, in the Edo period, and draws its water from the Tone River.

27
00:04:37,708 --> 00:04:39,939
[Vocab] 水路

28
00:04:40,339 --> 00:04:42,812
[Host] It means a waterway or canal.

29
00:04:43,411 --> 00:04:55,795
[Slow] 江戸が100万人の大きな町に成長できたのは、この用水が周りの米作りを支えたからだと言われています。

30
00:04:56,596 --> 00:05:04,300
[Host] It is said that Edo could grow into a city of one million people because this canal supported the rice farming around it.

31
00:05:04,899 --> 00:05:07,420
[Vocab] 成長

32
00:05:07,819 --> 00:05:09,596
[Host] It means growth.

33
00:05:10,196 --> 00:05:25,315
[Slow] 大阪府泉佐野市の「日根荘大木のかんがい用水群」は、中世の荘園で作られた水路が、今も大切に使われています。

34
00:05:26,115 --> 00:05:31,827
[Host] In Osaka, waterways built on a medieval manor are still carefully used today.

35
00:05:32,427 --> 00:05:34,803
[Vocab] 中世

36
00:05:35,204 --> 00:05:40,196
[Host] It means the Middle Ages — roughly the twelfth to sixteenth centuries in Japan.

37
00:05:40,795 --> 00:05:54,932
[Slow] 奈良県天理市の「崇神天皇陵堀」は、古墳の周りの堀の水を、農業のために利用してきた珍しい施設です。

38
00:05:55,732 --> 00:06:02,692
[Host] In Nara, the moat around an ancient burial mound has long provided water for farming — a rare case.

39
00:06:03,291 --> 00:06:05,403
[Vocab] 古墳

40
00:06:05,803 --> 00:06:11,516
[Host] It means an ancient burial mound, built for rulers over a thousand years ago.

41
00:06:12,115 --> 00:06:23,947
[Slow] 昔の人の知恵が作った水の道は、何百年もたった今も、日本の農業を支え続けています。

42
00:06:24,747 --> 00:06:32,475
[Host] The water paths built by the wisdom of people long ago still keep supporting Japan's farming, hundreds of years later.

43
00:06:33,076 --> 00:06:35,043
[Vocab] 知恵

44
00:06:35,444 --> 00:06:37,220
[Host] It means wisdom.

